      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 套期会计 · Principles-based effectiveness testing, converged with IFRS 9's post-2013 approach · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Aligning the accounting for a hedging relationship with its risk management purpose</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 24 governs HEDGE ACCOUNTING — a SPECIAL set of RULES permitting the RECOGNITION of GAINS and LOSSES on a HEDGING instrument and a HEDGED item TOGETHER, in the SAME period, WHERE a QUALIFYING hedging RELATIONSHIP exists. The Standard is BROADLY converged with IFRS 9'S OWN (post-2013) principles-BASED hedge accounting MODEL internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Three Hedge Types</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Fair value, cash flow, and net investment hedges</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Hedge type</span><span>Exposure being hedged</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Fair value hedge</span><span>EXPOSURE to CHANGES in the FAIR value of a RECOGNISED asset, LIABILITY, or FIRM commitment</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Cash flow hedge</span><span>EXPOSURE to VARIABILITY in CASH flows FROM a RECOGNISED asset/liability or a HIGHLY probable FORECAST transaction</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Net investment hedge</span><span>EXPOSURE to FOREIGN currency RISK on a NET investment in a FOREIGN operation</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Fair Value Hedges</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Both the hedged item and the hedging instrument adjusted through profit or loss</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">IN a FAIR VALUE hedge, the GAIN or LOSS on the HEDGING instrument is RECOGNISED in PROFIT or LOSS, WITH the CARRYING amount of the HEDGED item ALSO adjusted for the GAIN or LOSS ATTRIBUTABLE to the HEDGED risk, ALSO recognised in PROFIT or loss — the TWO offsetting EACH other to the EXTENT the HEDGE is EFFECTIVE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Cash Flow Hedges</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Effective portion in OCI, ineffective portion to profit or loss</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">IN a CASH flow hedge, the EFFECTIVE portion of the GAIN or LOSS on the HEDGING instrument is RECOGNISED WITHIN OTHER comprehensive INCOME, WHILE the INEFFECTIVE portion is RECOGNISED immediately in PROFIT or loss — the ACCUMULATED amount WITHIN OCI is SUBSEQUENTLY reclassified to PROFIT or loss WHEN the HEDGED forecast TRANSACTION affects PROFIT or loss.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Net Investment Hedges in Foreign Operations</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Accounted for similarly to cash flow hedges</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A HEDGE of a NET investment in a FOREIGN operation is ACCOUNTED for SIMILARLY to a CASH flow hedge — the EFFECTIVE portion RECOGNISED WITHIN other COMPREHENSIVE income, RECLASSIFIED to PROFIT or loss ON disposal of the FOREIGN operation (see the COMPANION ASBE No. 19 poster).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Hedge Effectiveness — a Principles-Based Approach</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">An economic relationship, not a rigid quantitative band</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A HEDGING relationship QUALIFIES for HEDGE accounting WHERE THERE is an ECONOMIC relationship BETWEEN the HEDGED item and the HEDGING instrument, CREDIT risk does NOT DOMINATE the VALUE changes RESULTING from that ECONOMIC relationship, and the HEDGE RATIO is CONSISTENT with the ENTITY'S actual RISK management STRATEGY.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Ending the Old Bright-Line 80–125% Testing</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A more flexible, judgement-based effectiveness assessment</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">THIS principles-BASED effectiveness TEST replaced an OLDER, more RIGID quantitative APPROACH — REQUIRING a HEDGE'S actual EFFECTIVENESS to fall WITHIN a SPECIFIC numerical BAND (COMMONLY 80%–125%) EACH period — a RETROSPECTIVE, bright-LINE test that OFTEN failed ECONOMICALLY sound HEDGES on TECHNICAL grounds. The CURRENT, more FLEXIBLE approach MIRRORS IFRS 9'S own 2013-era REFORM of hedge ACCOUNTING internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — a Cash Flow Hedge of Forecast Purchases</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Deferring the effective portion within OCI</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Hedging a highly probable foreign currency purchase</div><div class="wk-body">A company enters a forward contract to hedge a highly probable USD 5,000,000 purchase of raw materials expected in 6 months. At the reporting date, the forward contract shows a gain of RMB 300,000, assessed as fully effective.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises the RMB 300,000 gain WITHIN OTHER comprehensive INCOME — NOT profit or LOSS — DEFERRING it until the HEDGED forecast PURCHASE actually OCCURS and AFFECTS profit or LOSS.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — a Fair Value Hedge of a Fixed-Rate Loan</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Offsetting gains and losses within the same period's profit or loss</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Swapping fixed-rate exposure to floating</div><div class="wk-body">A company issues a fixed-rate loan and enters an interest rate swap to hedge against fair value changes due to interest rate movements. During the period, the swap gains RMB 400,000 in fair value, while the loan's fair value (attributable to interest rate risk) falls by RMB 380,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises the RMB 400,000 SWAP gain and the RMB 380,000 LOAN fair value LOSS BOTH in PROFIT or loss FOR the SAME period, LARGELY offsetting EACH other, REFLECTING the HEDGE'S effectiveness.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 24 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Risk management strategy and objectives for undertaking hedges</span><span>Amounts recognised in profit or loss and other comprehensive income for each hedge type</span><span>Hedge ineffectiveness recognised during the period</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a genuine economic relationship exists between the hedged item and hedging instrument</span><span>Whether a forecast transaction is genuinely "highly probable" for cash flow hedge purposes</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of hedging instruments and the hedged risk component</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 9</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 24 vs IFRS 9's hedge accounting model</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 24</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 9</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Effectiveness testing</span><span>Principles-based economic relationship test</span><span>Principles-based economic relationship test — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Three hedge types</span><span>Fair value, cash flow, net investment</span><span>Fair value, cash flow, net investment — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard — CHINA adopted the MORE flexible, PRINCIPLES-based hedge ACCOUNTING approach CLOSELY in step with IFRS 9'S own 2013-era REFORM.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every hedge accounting event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Fair value hedge gain/loss</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Both hedging instrument and hedged item adjusted through profit or loss</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Cash flow hedge effective portion</span><span><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span></span><span>Deferred in OCI until the hedged transaction affects profit or loss</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 19</span><span>Foreign Currency Translation — relevant for net investment hedges of foreign operations</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 22</span><span>Recognition and Measurement of Financial Instruments — supplies the classification of hedging instruments</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Hedge effectiveness</div><div class="glossary-def">The extent to which changes in the fair value or cash flows of a hedging instrument offset changes in the hedged item, assessed through an economic-relationship test.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Hedge ratio</div><div class="glossary-def">The relationship between the quantity of the hedging instrument and the quantity of the hedged item, required to be consistent with actual risk management strategy.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) <span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) <span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) <span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe24 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
